{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.DescartesKnotEigenbasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.DescartesKnotEigenbasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRep","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.GenericParameter","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovTraceInstance"],"declarations":99,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_particle_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_particle_count","kind":"theorem","line":1007,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L1007-L1010","doc":"**Corollary**: the number of particle species at level n is finite\nand equals ⌊n/2⌋ + 1 — each species is a knot type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_eigenvalues_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_eigenvalues_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":999,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L999-L1005","doc":"**Corollary**: the eigenvalues q and -q⁻¹ of the R-matrix braiding\nare always distinct in a Descartes universe, ensuring the Hecke\nalgebra quotient is well-defined and the braid representation\nis faithful. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sigma_separates_n3_channels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sigma_separates_n3_channels","kind":"theorem","line":978,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L978-L997","doc":"**`σ₁` separates the two `n = 3` summands, in every Descartes universe.**\n\nThe positive counterpart to `jones_channels_not_separating`, and the\nreason that negative is narrow: the difference is `q⁻¹`, and `q > 0`\nforces `q⁻¹ ≠ 0`, so there is no Descartes `q` at which these two\ncharacters agree — including the `q*` where the two *Jones values* do.\n\nSo \"both summands are detected\" is not out of reach; it needs the\ndetector attached to its summand, which is what\n`DescartesMarkovTrace.trSummand` is for. What remains is to construct\n`trSummand` from the Hoefsmit values rather than leave it free — a\nformalisation of the seminormal representation, not a further open\nquestion about the mathematics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitOffDiag_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitOffDiag_pos","kind":"theorem","line":972,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L972-L976","doc":"The gauge is non-singular: `√(1 + q² + q⁴)/(1 + q²) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma2_conj_S1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma2_conj_S1","kind":"theorem","line":953,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L953-L970","doc":"**The orthogonal and square-root-free seminormal forms are conjugate**, by\nthe diagonal gauge `diag(b, 1)`:\n\n  `ρ(σ₂) · diag(b,1) = diag(b,1) · S1`.\n\nStated without inverses. `hoefsmitOffDiag q > 0`, so the gauge is\ninvertible and this is a genuine similarity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma1_eq_S0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma1_eq_S0","kind":"theorem","line":946,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L946-L951","doc":"**`rhoMixedSigma1` is the library's `S0`.** Recorded so the duplication is\nvisible in the code and not only in a commit message. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitGauge","kind":"def","line":941,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L941-L944","doc":"The diagonal gauge `diag(b, 1)` taking the library's square-root-free `S1`\nto the orthogonal form the compute returns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixed_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixed_braid","kind":"theorem","line":884,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L884-L908","doc":"**The braid relation** `ρ(σ₁)ρ(σ₂)ρ(σ₁) = ρ(σ₂)ρ(σ₁)ρ(σ₂)`.\n\nTogether with the two quadratic relations above, this is what makes the\npair a representation of `H_3(q)` rather than two matrices that happen to\nhave the right traces — and hence what makes `charMixedSigma` a\n*character*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma2_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma2_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":859,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L859-L882","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation for `ρ_[2,1](σ₂)`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma1_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma1_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":849,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L849-L857","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation for `ρ_[2,1](σ₁)`**:\n`σ² = (q − q⁻¹)·σ + 1`, equivalently `(σ − q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.det_rhoMixedSigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.det_rhoMixedSigma2","kind":"theorem","line":832,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L832-L847","doc":"**The determinant of `ρ_[2,1](σ₂)` is `−1`** — the product of the two\nHecke eigenvalues `q · (−q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.trace_rhoMixedSigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.trace_rhoMixedSigma2","kind":"theorem","line":816,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L816-L830","doc":"`ρ_[2,1](σ₂)` has the same trace as `ρ_[2,1](σ₁)`, namely `q − q⁻¹`.\n\nForced: `σ₁` and `σ₂` are conjugate in the braid group, and conjugate\nelements have equal character. Here it falls out of the closed forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.charSymmetricSigma_sub_charMixedSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.charSymmetricSigma_sub_charMixedSigma","kind":"theorem","line":801,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L801-L804","doc":"**The two `n = 3` channel characters differ by exactly `q⁻¹`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.charMixedSigma_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.charMixedSigma_eq","kind":"theorem","line":796,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L796-L799","doc":"The mixed character evaluates to `q − q⁻¹` — derived from the matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.charSymmetricSigma_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.charSymmetricSigma_eq","kind":"theorem","line":792,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L792-L794","doc":"The symmetric character evaluates to `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.charMixedSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.charMixedSigma","kind":"def","line":786,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L786-L790","doc":"Character of the mixed-symmetry (spin-1/2) summand `λ = [2,1]` on `σ₁` at\n`n = 3` — **the trace of `ρ_[2,1](σ₁)`**, not an asserted value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.charSymmetricSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.charSymmetricSigma","kind":"def","line":779,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L779-L784","doc":"Character of the symmetric (spin-3/2) summand `λ = [3]` on `σ₁` at\n`n = 3`. The representation is one-dimensional and sends each generator\nto `q`, so the character is its `1 × 1` trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma2","kind":"def","line":773,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L773-L777","doc":"`ρ_[2,1](σ₂)` in the Hoefsmit seminormal basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rhoMixedSigma1","kind":"def","line":767,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L767-L771","doc":"`ρ_[2,1](σ₁)` in the Hoefsmit seminormal basis: diagonal, eigenvalues `q`\nand `−q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitOffDiag_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitOffDiag_sq","kind":"theorem","line":759,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L759-L765","doc":"The radicand of `hoefsmitOffDiag` is non-negative, so the square root is\nhonest and `hoefsmitOffDiag q ^ 2` recovers it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.one_add_sq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.one_add_sq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":756,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L756-L757","doc":"`1 + q² > 0`, so it is safe as a denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitOffDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hoefsmitOffDiag","kind":"def","line":751,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L751-L754","doc":"The off-diagonal Hoefsmit entry `√(1 + q² + q⁴)/(1 + q²)` of `ρ_[2,1](σ₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jones_channels_not_separating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jones_channels_not_separating","kind":"theorem","line":677,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L677-L695","doc":"**There is a Descartes universe in which the two `n = 3` channel values\nare equal.**\n\nThe headline consequence of the two results above, and the reason\n`descartes_n3_both_detected` is scoped to non-vanishing: at this `q` the\nunknot's symmetric-channel value and the trefoil's mixed-channel value are\nthe *same real number*, so exhibiting both non-zero says nothing about the\ntwo summands being distinguished.\n\nNumerically `q ≈ 0.7795446638`, both channels `≈ -2.0623447988` (50 dps).\nSeparating the channels needs `DescartesMarkovTrace.trSummand`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jonesSymmetric_eq_jonesMixed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jonesSymmetric_eq_jonesMixed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L665-L675","doc":"The reduction the docstring above describes, **proved** rather than\nasserted: over `q > 0`, the two channel values agree exactly when the\nquintic vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jones_channels_coincide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jones_channels_coincide","kind":"theorem","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L633-L663","doc":"**The two `n = 3` channel values coincide at a `q` the Descartes\ncondition permits**, so non-vanishing of each does *not* establish that\nthe two summands are distinguished.\n\n`jonesSymmetric D = jonesMixed D` reduces, over `q > 0`, to\n`q⁵ - q⁴ + q³ + q² - 1 = 0`, which is negative at `q = 7/10` and positive\nat `q = 4/5`; the intermediate value theorem supplies a root between.\nNumerically the root is `q ≈ 0.779544663820934968877573423932`, where both\nchannels take the value `≈ -2.0623447988` (verified at 50 decimal digits).\n\nSuch a `q` satisfies `0 < q` and `q ≠ 1`, so it is a legitimate Descartes\nparameter. At it, the pair `(jonesSymmetric, jonesMixed)` carries no more\ninformation than a single number.\n\nThis is why `descartes_n3_both_detected` is scoped to non-vanishing:\nseparating the channels needs the values attached to their summands, i.e.\n`DescartesMarkovTrace.trSummand`, not two reals that happen to be\nnon-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_n3_both_detected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_n3_both_detected","kind":"theorem","line":604,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L604-L631","doc":"**Corollary**: for `n = 3` in a Descartes universe, the symmetric and\nmixed-symmetry channel values are each non-zero — the unknot's value in\nthe spin-3/2 channel and the trefoil's in the spin-1/2 channel.\n\nStated over the two **named** values. Until 2026-09-04 this was\n`∃ (j_sym j_mix : ℝ), j_sym ≠ 0 ∧ j_mix ≠ 0`, which is a property of `ℝ`:\nthe two Jones values, and `n = 3`, and the two channels, appeared only in\nthe proof term and the comments. The proof was real work; the statement\nrecorded none of it.\n\n**This does not say the two channels are separated** — see\n`jones_channels_coincide` below, which shows they take the *same* value at\na `q` the Descartes condition permits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jonesMixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jonesMixed","kind":"def","line":598,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L598-L602","doc":"Jones value of the trefoil in the mixed-symmetry (spin-1/2) channel at\n`n = 3`: `J = -q⁻⁴(1 - q² + q⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jonesSymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jonesSymmetric","kind":"def","line":593,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L593-L596","doc":"Jones value of the unknot in the symmetric (spin-3/2) channel at `n = 3`:\n`J = -(q + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_knot_eigenbasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_knot_eigenbasis","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L551-L591","doc":"The Descartes condition (q > 0, q ≠ 1, q not a root of unity)\nis sufficient to construct the full knot eigenbasis data.\n\nThe key inputs:\n- Semisimplicity of H_n(q) ← q not a root of unity (Jimbo's theorem)\n- Eigenvalue distinctness ← q > 0 and q ≠ 1\n- Markov trace existence ← Jones's construction (1987)\n- Alexander surjectivity ← classical topology (Alexander, 1923)\n\nAll four are available for any Descartes universe.\n\n**The witness is trivial, and the statement now says so.** The previous\nversion's conclusion was `∀ (_ : Fin numSummands), ∃ jonesVal, jonesVal\n< 0` — the summand index discarded and the value tied to nothing — and\nit was proved by exhibiting the symmetric-channel Jones value\n`-(q + q⁻¹)`, once, for every index. The docstring described that as \"a\ngenuine, `q`-dependent detector\"; the *type* accepted any negative real\nand would have accepted the same one for all summands, which is what the\nproof did.\n\nThe conclusion is now stated over `trSummand`, so the index occurs. The\nwitness constructed below is deliberately the trivial one\n(`trSummand n i x = x`), because that is all this file can supply: the\nper-summand character values for general `n` are upstream. Nothing here\nclaims otherwise any more. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:descartes-knot-eigenbasis","label":"cor:descartes-knot-eigenbasis","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.all_summands_detected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.all_summands_detected","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L547-L547","doc":"Each summand at each level is detected by the Markov trace — stated\nover `markov.trSummand`, so the summand index occurs in the body and\nthe detected value is the trace's component in *that* summand rather\nthan a free real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.schurWeyl_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.schurWeyl_level","kind":"theorem","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L542-L542","doc":"Consistency: the decomposition returned at level `n` is a\ndecomposition of `V^⊗n`.\n\nMissing until 2026-09-04, so `schurWeyl n hn` could return the\ndecomposition of any *other* level and nothing noticed. The sibling\n`QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition` carries the analogous `n_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.markov","kind":"def","line":535,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L535-L535","doc":"Markov trace on the Hecke tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.braidRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.braidRep","kind":"def","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L533-L533","doc":"Braid representation at each level n ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.schurWeyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.schurWeyl","kind":"def","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L531-L531","doc":"Schur-Weyl decomposition at each level n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":529,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L529-L529","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesKnotEigenbasis","kind":"structure","line":518,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L518-L549","doc":"**Descartes knot eigenbasis completeness.**\n\nA Descartes universe provides all the data needed for knot\neigenbasis completeness: the Hecke algebra (from the R-matrix),\nthe Schur-Weyl decomposition (from semisimplicity), and the\nMarkov trace (from Jones's construction).\n\nThis is the instantiation theorem that bridges the abstract\n`KnotEigenbasisData` structure (Chapter 4) with the concrete\nDescartes universe (Chapter 6). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartesMarkovTrace_z_arbitrary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartesMarkovTrace_z_arbitrary","kind":"theorem","line":490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L490-L514","doc":"**`DescartesMarkovTrace.z` carries no information**: every non-zero real is\nthe `z` of some instance.\n\nMachine-checked demonstration of the supersession note above. `z` occurs in\nits own declaration and in `z_ne_zero` and nowhere else, so it is not the\nMarkov parameter of anything — the structure never relates it to `tr`.\nContrast `descartesWtrace_markov`, where `z_D = q³/(q²+1)` appears in the\nconclusion because it is forced.\n\nRecorded as a theorem so a later reader cannot mistake the field for a\nconstraint, and so re-introducing a free `z` after a repair fails against a\nstanding counterexample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtrace_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtrace_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L477-L488","doc":"**The Descartes Markov trace is the sum of its per-shape summands.**\n\nThe decomposition `DescartesMarkovTrace` never states: the trace is not an\nopaque functional with a detached list of numbers beside it, it *is* the\nweighted sum over partitions of `n+1`. Together with `descartesWtrace_markov`\nthis is the whole content the structure was standing in for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtraceSummand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtraceSummand","kind":"def","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L461-L475","doc":"**The per-summand component of the Descartes Markov trace.**\n\n`W_ν · tr ρ_ν(x)` — the Ocneanu weight at `z_D = q³/(q²+1)` times the\ncharacter of the seminormal representation on the shape `ν`. This is the\nreal object `DescartesMarkovTrace.trSummand` gestures at: indexed by Young\ndiagrams of size `n+1` rather than by `Fin (n/2+1)`, evaluated on an\nelement of the Hecke algebra rather than on a natural number, and carrying\nthe weight rather than asserting a value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtrace_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtrace_markov","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L402-L416","doc":"**The Markov property holds for every Descartes universe**:\n`tr(ι y · σₙ) = z_D · tr(y)` with `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`.\n\nThis is the property `DescartesMarkovTrace` is named for and does not\ncontain. Nothing is assumed here — the library proves it, and the\nDescartes hypotheses discharge what it asks for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartesWtrace","kind":"def","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L390-L400","doc":"**The Markov trace of a Descartes universe** — the real one.\n\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtrace` at the Descartes parameter, available\nbecause `descartes_notRootOfUnity` discharges its genericity hypothesis. It\nis a linear functional on the actual Hecke algebra, its λ-sum carries the\nOcneanu weights, and it satisfies the Markov property at `z_D` — the three\nthings `DescartesMarkovTrace` above lacks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_sq_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_sq_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L384-L388","doc":"`q² ≠ 1` — the `m = 2` instance of `descartes_notRootOfUnity`.\n\n**Not** the hypothesis `wtrace` takes; see the docstring of `descartesWtrace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_sq_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_sq_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L380-L382","doc":"`q² + 1 ≠ 0` over `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_notRootOfUnity_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_notRootOfUnity_sq","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L373-L378","doc":"The genericity the library's weight lemmas ask for, in the `q²` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_notRootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descartes_notRootOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L355-L371","doc":"**A Descartes parameter is not a root of unity.**\n\n`DescartesData` gives `0 < q` and `q ≠ 1`; over `ℝ` that is already the\nlibrary's `NotRootOfUnity`, since a positive real with `qᵐ = 1` for some\n`m > 0` must be `1`. This is the hypothesis `wtrace` needs, so every\nDescartes universe admits the genuine Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.summand_detection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.summand_detection","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L313-L313","doc":"Every irreducible summand is detected: for each level `n` and each\nsummand index `i`, some element has non-zero trace **in that\nsummand**.\n\n`i` occurs in the body. It did not until 2026-09-04 — see the module\ndocstring for what the previous form asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.tr_eq_sum_summands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.tr_eq_sum_summands","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L304-L304","doc":"The components decompose the trace:\n`tr n x = Σ_{i < ⌊n/2⌋+1} trSummand n i x`.\n\nThis is what stops `trSummand` from being free data an instance may\nchoose independently of `tr`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.trSummand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.trSummand","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L298-L298","doc":"Component of the trace in the summand indexed by `i` at level `n`.\n\nWithout this the decomposition is invisible to the trace, and no\nstatement can be made *per summand* — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.tr_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.tr_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L293-L293","doc":"The trace of the identity is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L291-L291","doc":"The trace functional on H_n(q) elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L289-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.z","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L288-L288","doc":"The Markov parameter z = -(q - q⁻¹)⁻¹ · q^(1/2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L286-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesMarkovTrace","kind":"structure","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L283-L314","doc":"**Markov trace** on the Hecke algebra tower of a Descartes universe.\nThe trace exists, is unique, and detects every irreducible summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.far_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.far_comm","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L277-L277","doc":"Far commutativity: σᵢσⱼ = σⱼσᵢ for |i - j| ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L272-L272","doc":"σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂ (braid relation for adjacent generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.grp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.grp","kind":"def","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L270-L270","doc":"Braid group structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.faithful","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L267-L267","doc":"Faithfulness: distinct braids give distinct traces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.trace_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.trace_of","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L265-L265","doc":"The representation ρ_n assigns each braid to an automorphism\nof V^⊗n, encoded here as a real number (trace in the\nfundamental representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.sigma","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L261-L261","doc":"Braid generators σ_1, ..., σ_{n-1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.BraidType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.BraidType","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L259-L259","doc":"Braid type (abstract B_n). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.n_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.n_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.n","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L256-L256","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep.mk","kind":"ctor","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L254-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidRep","kind":"structure","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L248-L279","doc":"**Faithful braid representation** ρ_n : B_n → Aut_C(V^⊗n) from\nthe Descartes braided monoidal structure.\n\nFaithfulness for n = 3 follows from the distinct eigenvalues\nof the R-matrix (q ≠ -q⁻¹), which is guaranteed by q > 0, q ≠ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.schur_weyl_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.schur_weyl_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L241-L244","doc":"The Schur-Weyl decomposition always has at least one summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.schur_weyl_n3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.schur_weyl_n3","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L235-L239","doc":"The Schur-Weyl decomposition at n = 3 has 2 summands:\nspin 3/2 (symmetric) and spin 1/2 (mixed symmetry). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.summandOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.summandOf","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L233-L233","doc":"Projection: every vector projects to a unique summand index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.max_spin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.max_spin","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L230-L230","doc":"Maximum spin is n/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.spinLabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.spinLabel","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L228-L228","doc":"Spin labels for each summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.summands_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.summands_count","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L226-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.numSummands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.numSummands","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L225-L225","doc":"Number of irreducible summands = ⌊n/2⌋ + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.tensorPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.tensorPower","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L223-L223","doc":"V^⊗n as a type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.n","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L221-L221","doc":"Number of tensor factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl.mk","kind":"ctor","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesSchurWeyl","kind":"structure","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L211-L233","doc":"**Schur-Weyl data** for a Descartes universe at level n.\n\nFor C = Rep(SU_q(2)) with V the spin-1/2 representation:\nV^⊗n ≅ ⊕_{j} V_j ⊗ S_j where j ranges over spins\nn/2, n/2 - 1, ..., 1/2 or 0 (partitions with ≤ 2 parts).\n\nThe number of summands is ⌊n/2⌋ + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eigenvalues_distinct_of_descartes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eigenvalues_distinct_of_descartes","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L202-L207","doc":"For q > 0, the eigenvalues q and -q⁻¹ are distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.eigenvalues_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.eigenvalues_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L200-L200","doc":"Eigenvalues are distinct (q ≠ -q⁻¹ when q > 0, q ≠ 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.eigenvalue_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.eigenvalue_neg","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L198-L198","doc":"The negative braiding eigenvalue -q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.eigenvalue_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.eigenvalue_pos","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L196-L196","doc":"The positive braiding eigenvalue q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.one","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L194-L194","doc":"Unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.mul","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L192-L192","doc":"Multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.T","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L190-L190","doc":"The generators T_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.carrier","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L188-L188","doc":"Carrier of H_n(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.n_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.n_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.n","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L185-L185","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L183-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesHeckeAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L176-L200","doc":"The Hecke algebra H_n(q) constructed from the R-matrix of\nU_q(su(2)) in a Descartes universe.\n\nThe braiding c_{V,V} has eigenvalues q and -q⁻¹.\nThe quadratic relation (T_i - q)(T_i + q⁻¹) = 0 defines\nthe Hecke algebra as a quotient of the braid group algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L170-L172","doc":"q > 0 implies q ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.genus_is_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.genus_is_four","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L165-L168","doc":"The genus of a Descartes universe is 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.dimV_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.dimV_eq","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L163-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.dimV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.dimV","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L162-L162","doc":"Dimension of V (forced to 2 by the volume constraint). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.euler_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.euler_eq","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L160-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L159-L159","doc":"Euler characteristic is -6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L157-L157","doc":"q ≠ 1 (non-classical deformation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L155-L155","doc":"q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.q","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L153-L153","doc":"Deformation parameter q from U_q(su(2)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesData","kind":"structure","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean#L150-L163","doc":"Descartes condition: χ(A) = -6 with 6 invertible. ","signatureChunk":0}]}